expect: written
note: written
keeps: percent
bars: and exports from version 3 (as )?a fraction | and later ones (as )?a fraction | and later exports (as )?a fraction | and newer ones (as )?a fraction | and newer exports (as )?a fraction
why: run 16 wrote a sentence whose second clause borrowed the first clause's verb, and it had to be read twice to parse; each clause names its verb, as "exports from version 3 write it as a fraction"
labelled: 2026-09-29
--- code
export function readRate(entry: LedgerEntry): number {
  return entry.rate > 1 ? entry.rate / 100 : entry.rate;
}
--- facts
Exports before version 3 write the rate as a percentage and exports from version 3 a fraction.
This function therefore divides a rate above 1 by 100.
